  Bowmen  
 }}}01}}} 
----------
    38    
 152nd/A  
  Legion  
          
  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 110th Bowmen, the 209th Warg Riders, the 124th 
Skeletal Dragons, the 109th Heavy Cavalry, the 272nd Dragons and the 277th 
Eagles in reserve.  I stood determinedly at the head of my thousands.  
Dracona commanded a host of loyal soldiers into the battle.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Luckily for me, some mischievous bandits ambushed Dracona
's rearguard, giving me a clear advantage.  As the fierce struggle 
developed, the tactical wit of Dracona and I seemed to be evenly matched and 
neither leader could achieve a tactical advantage.
  The Dragons I led were rendered worthless by their intolerance of Guerin.  
I could make almost no use of the Eagles, who could not comprehend my 
military strategy.
  Across the whole front, the Veteran 108th Skeletal Bowmen were arrayed 
against the 152nd Legion.  The 240th Bowmen outflanked the enemy and charged 
in with full strength.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons swooped down on the 152nd 
Legion and attacked them.  The 108th Skeletal Bowmen fought the 152nd Legion 
and determinedly plowed into their opponents.
  The battle ended victoriously for the soldiers of Guerin as they broke 
through at a critical moment.  The 240th Bowmen pursued the enemy and 
scattered the 152nd Legion in all directions.
  The Ark Royal Sea was overrun by the forces of Guerin.
  Midsummer's day came and went and a pleasant late summer arrived.  I 
recruited enough men in the Ark Royal Sea to form the 302nd Garrison for the 
army of the provincial garrison commander.
  During fall, I marched on the Falkland Sea (#1305) with my forces.

  A great host of savage warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll into the Forest province of the Falkland 
Sea, ruled by Isis (#89).  I commanded the attacking armies.  The defending 
forces were commanded by Isis.  The armies were drawn up into lines of 
battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of the Falkland Sea (1305):

