  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 272nd Dragons, the 109th Heavy Cavalry and the 277th 
Eagles in reserve.  Standing at the ready with my warriors was I.  Isis 
marched with her loyal troops, eyes set in grim determination.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  The two armies strived mightily for the high ground, and 
I obtained the edge by getting there first.  Further, in this chess match, I 
seemed to have the tactical upper hand.
  The Dragons I led were ineffective because of their poor relations with me.
I could make almost no use of the Eagles, who virtually ignored my military 
strategy.
  On the left outside flank, the Veteran 108th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 
150th Bowmen.  The 241st Bowmen outflanked the enemy lines and charged in 
with full strength.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons soared over the 150th Bowmen 
and attacked them.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons were decimated by the arrows 
loosed by the pesky Bowmen.  The 108th Skeletal Bowmen fought the 150th 
Bowmen and wasted no time in smashing their lines.
  Out on the right wing, the Crack 240th Bowmen were arrayed against the 
151st Fleet Marines.  The 110th Bowmen outflanked the undermanned enemy and 
attacked with full force.  The 240th Bowmen battled the 151st Fleet Marines 
and smashed them like rotten oranges.
  Having found a weak spot in the line of the host of Isis, a final savage 
slashing attack finished off their enemy and won the battle for me.  The 
108th Skeletal Bowmen destroyed the 150th Bowmen.  The 240th Bowmen 
annihilated the 151st Fleet Marines.
  Guerin's host ended the campaign successfully and conquered the province 
of the Falkland Sea.  The battle affected the quality of our forces:  we 
could not have been better satisfied with the fighting spirit of the 108th 
Skeletal Bowmen, and we have elevated its ranking to Crack.
  With the advent of the early winter season, I couldn't recruit Garrison in 
the Falkland Sea because there wasn't enough gold.  Instead, I practiced my 
Tactics well but could not improve my skill in Tactics.

  Thy humble servant,   Guerin


From: Teleko
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I boldly marched my forces into the Third Sea (#807).  Viewing 
the southwestern horizon, one can see a poor Mountain province known as the 
Albatross Sea (#708).  It is said that Kishijoten reigns there.  It is known 
to be occupied by Orcs.  Their Orcish fighters fight as Bowmen.  West of 
here lies the province of the Balearic Sea (#707), ruled by no one.  It is 
said to be a Sea province occupied by no races.  To the northwest lies a Sea 
area named the Moonshine Sea (#706), populated by no races.  It is ruled by 
no one.

  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Uga-Buga Makumbian empire 
marched on the Forest province of the Third Sea, a land defended by the 
soldiers of Presto.  I was in command of the invading armies.  The defending 
forces were commanded by Presto.  The armies were drawn up into lines of 
battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of the Third Sea (0807):

  269th             
  Bowmen            
 }}}01}}}           
                    
 96th/VS   270th/V  
  Bowmen    Bowmen  
 }}}01}}}  }}}01}}} 
--------------------
    73        73    
  88th/A    89th/A  
  Axemen    Axemen  
                    
  DEFENDING ARMY

  I led my armies into the fray.  Presto commanded a host of loyal soldiers.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  I was unlucky, for I had been unable to locate a 
protected encampment to rest my troops the previous day, thus my men were in 
dismal condition.  But my wise tactical planning assured my forces a clear 
superiority.

  Out on the left flank, the Veteran 96th Skeletal Bowmen were arrayed 
against the 88th Axemen.  The 269th Bowmen flanked the undermanned enemy 
lines and charged in with full strength.  On this battleground, the 88th 
Axemen were slightly disrupted by a slippery patch of ground and they 
entered the fight at a tiny disadvantage.  The 96th Skeletal Bowmen fought 
with the 88th Axemen and stout-heartedly advanced against them.
  On the right outside flank, the Veteran 270th Bowmen were arrayed against 
the 89th Axemen.  Here, the 270th Bowmen were at first slow to join battle, 
but when a brave little squire picked up a dagger and said "I'll show you 
how to fight!"  , they were so inspired that they determinedly charged into 
battle.  The 270th Bowmen fought with the 89th Axemen and gradually pushed 
them back.
  The forces of Teleko broke through and were victorious.  The 269th Bowmen 
pursued the enemy and demolished the 88th Axemen.
  Teleko's well-planned campaign accomplished the conquest of the Third Sea. 
The battle affected the quality of our forces:  we can raise the rating of 
the 269th Bowmen to Veteran, its men having displayed especially admirable 
courage.  The 89th Axemen were unable to retreat and were disbanded into the 
population.  Teleko's efforts raised my skill in Tactics.
  With the coming of the early summer season I announced a plea for recruits 
in the Third Sea and was able to form the 300th Garrison to fight for the 
provincial garrison commander.
  In late summer, I boldly marched my forces into the Buccaneer Sea (#806).  
Viewing the northwestern horizon, a man can see a prosperous Sea province 
known as the Valiant Sea (#805).  It is said that no one reigns there.  It 
is known to be populated by Whales.  If need be, they can muster a host of 
Whales to defend their province.

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll's forces initiated a campaign of 
conquest in the Buccaneer Sea, a Forest province owing allegiance to the 
provincial garrison commander.  I commanded the attacking armies.  The 
defending forces were commanded by the provincial garrison commander.  The 
armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of the Buccaneer Sea (0806):

  270th             
  Bowmen            
 }}}01}}}           
                    
 269th/V   96th/VS  
  Bowmen    Bowmen  
 }}}01}}}  }}}01}}} 
--------------------
 GC  }}}GC}}} 
  87th/A    86th/A  
 Marines    Bowmen  
                    
  DEFENDING ARMY

  I marched with my loyal troops, jaws set in grim resolution.  No generals 
were present to lead the forces of the acting commander.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Teleko's luck didn't hold up this time.  My superstitious 
men became unsettled when my priests were unable to properly sacrifice a 
goat to the Great Father because they had all been slain by gryphons.  On 
the other hand my clever tactical maneuvers gave my forces an undeniable 
advantage.

  On the left wing, the Veteran 269th Bowmen were arrayed against the 87th 
Fleet Marines.  The 270th Bowmen outflanked the enemy and charged in with 
full strength.  The 269th Bowmen battled with the 87th Fleet Marines and 
mowed them down like weeds.
  On the right outside flank, the Veteran 96th Skeletal Bowmen were arrayed 
against the 86th Bowmen.  In this match, the 86th Bowmen advanced 
confidently, but were thrown into disarray when a hidden battery of 
catapults unexpectedly opened up.
  But might defeat now be snatched from the jaws of victory?  The 96th 
Skeletal Bowmen had to cross a ditch, which disordered the 96th Skeletal 
Bowmen and caused some confusion.  Even so, the 96th Skeletal Bowmen fought 
with the 86th Bowmen and stout-heartedly advanced against them.
  Teleko's great horde overpowered the army of the acting commander and took 
the field, scattering their enemies.  The 269th Bowmen slew the 87th Fleet 
Marines almost to a man.  The 96th Skeletal Bowmen scattered the 86th Bowmen 
in all directions.
  The Buccaneer Sea was overrun by Teleko's men in a hard-fought campaign.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into fall.  I couldn't recruit Garrison 
in the Buccaneer Sea because there wasn't enough gold.  Instead, I practiced 
my Thievery well but could not improve my Thievery.
  During early winter, I failed in my ineffectual attempt to cast a Skeletal 
Army spell.

  Thy humble servant,   Teleko


From: Gridley, Squire to Melantheus
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, Melantheus prepared to quench his 
thirst for adventure.  He rode into the Dolphin Sea.  During his travels 
this season, an Elemental Sorceror rushed at Melantheus like a bolt from the 
blue.  He spoke to the Elemental Sorceror with respectful words, and combat 
was averted.

  Melantheus heard a rumor telling of a feature in Khurum (#903) previously 
unknown to us, a Hollow Tree where dwells the Centaur.  The Hollow Tree is 
reputed to contain the Invisible Sword.
  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  Melantheus tried to practice 
his Sageness, but the task seemed beyond his natural aptitude.  He 
discovered nothing valuable in his sagely experiments.
  With the advent of the late summer season, Melantheus tried to practice 
his Sageness, but the task seemed beyond his ability.  He discovered nothing 
in his sagely researches.
  With the coming of the fall season Melantheus tried to improve his 
Sageness, but the task seemed beyond his aptitude.  He discovered nothing 
worthy of note in his sagely researches.
  With the advent of the early winter season Melantheus was instructed in 
Sageness by Lallipugh.  Melantheus practiced his Sageness and improved 
substantially.  He discovered nothing worthy of note in his sagely 
researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Gridley, Squire to Melantheus


From: Tao-Li
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter gave way to fragrant spring.  I recruited enough men in the 
Jellyfish Sea to create the 296th Fleet, the 297th Axemen and the 298th 
Garrison for the army of Tao-Li.
  During early summer, I sailed into Mare Ionium (#1104) with my command.  
To the northeast there lies a Desert province known as Bir Nzaran (#1203), a 
prosperous land of Dwarves where Alaric rules.  Their Dwarven fighters 
prefer to fight as Axemen and Heavy Cavalry.  East of here is the Callisto 
Sea (#1204), a Sea province owned by no one, where no races dwell.  Looking 
to the northwest, one can see a prosperous Sea area, which is known as the 
Angel Sea (#1103).  It is populated by Whales and no one rules there.  If 
need be, they can muster an army of Whales to defend their province.
  Tao-Li's forces encountered little opposition in Mare Ionium and I there 
established our reign.  Mare Ionium was discovered to have an income of 3 
gold.
  With the coming of the late summer season, I moved into the Callisto Sea 
(#1204) with my Fleet.  To the northeast lies a rich Forest province named 
Bronzeleaf (#1303), populated by Humans.  It is ruled by no one.  Their 
Human warriors fight as Legion.  East of here lies the province of Mercia 
(#1304), ruled by no one.  It is known to be a Sea province occupied by 
Whales.  If need be, they can call on an army of Whales to defend their 
province.
  Tao-Li's forces conquered the Callisto Sea without any major battles.  The 
Callisto Sea was found to have a tax base of 1 gold.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into fall.  I attempted an illegal 
move.  I was ordered to move from the Callisto Sea to Mercia, further than 
my navy could move.  So, I practiced enthusiastically and improved my 
ability in Thievery.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  I tried to move from the 
Callisto Sea to Mammoth, a non-adjacent province.  This is illegal!  So, I 
worked hard on my Psychic Magic but was frustrated in my self-improvement 
efforts.

  Thy humble servant,   Tao-Li


From: Lallipugh
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Raiden (#96) rebuffed Lallipugh's offer of employment, 
ridiculing Uga-Buga Makumb's alignment and saying "That Uga-Buga Makumb is 
the most infamous despot in the land!"  After talking to Raiden, I judged 
him (a Human well known for Tactics) to have a Good, Brave nature.
  With the coming of the early summer season, I moved into the Dolphin Sea.  
I encountered no monsters.
  Midsummer's night came and went and late summer arrived.  I tried to 
improve my Sageness, but the task was beyond my aptitude.  I discovered 
nothing worthy of note in my sagely researches.
  With the advent of the fall season I tried to improve my Sageness, but the 
task was beyond my natural ability.  I invented nothing valuable in my 
sagely experiments.
  With the coming of the early winter season, I practiced hard for many 
weeks and my skill in Sageness increased.  I invented nothing valuable in my 
sagely researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Lallipugh


From: Watson, Squire to Amalric
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter melted into fragrant spring.  Amalric enlisted enough men in 
Mare Tarkium to create the 293rd Dragons for the army of Uga-Buga Makumb.
  During early summer, Amalric rode into the Dolphin Sea.
  With the advent of the late summer season, Amalric was instructed in 
Sageness by Lallipugh.  Amalric practiced his Sageness and his skill in 
Sageness went up.  He invented nothing worthy of note in his sagely 
researches.
  The summer surrendered to fall.  Amalric invented nothing in his sagely 
researches.
  During early winter, Amalric was tutored in the art of Sageness by 
Lallipugh.  Amalric practiced his Sageness and improved noticeably.  He 
discovered nothing worthy of note in his sagely researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Watson, Squire to Amalric


From: Odysseus
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I announced a call for recruits in the Virgo Sea and was able to 
enlist the 287th Garrison and the 288th Garrison to fight for me.
  Windy spring was followed by a fragrant early summer.  I marched on the 
Jellyfish Sea (#1105) with my formidable command.  I discovered a previously 
unheard of Cave (#104) in the Jellyfish Sea, inhabited by the Medusa.  What 
treasure may lie there is unknown.  Hardened adventurers fear the Medusa 
because she is a hateful creature resembling an ugly woman who has slimy, 
writhing snakes in the place of hair.  Her gaze has been known to turn even 
a hero to stone.
  With the advent of the late summer season I dropped off the 287th Garrison 
and the 288th Garrison in the Jellyfish Sea for the provincial garrison 
commander.
  The hot days of summer mellowed into fall.  I travelled to the Dolphin Sea.
  During early winter, I discovered nothing in my sagely experiments.

  Thy humble servant,   Odysseus


From: Montgomery, Squire to Elmer
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the fall season Elmer journeyed to the Mermaid Sea.  He 
encountered no monster.
  The fall cooled into a frigid early winter.  Elmer moved into the Dolphin 
Sea.  He saw no wandering monster.

  Thy humble servant,   Montgomery, Squire to Elmer


